{
  "assessment": "The change introduces three new output sinks (`errors.py`, `logfile.py`, `metrics.py`) that format event data for different destinations. Each sink implements a `render(event)` function that directly serializes raw event metadata into strings or JSON without invoking any sanitization routine. This leaves the service in the same insecure state as the other unscrubbed sink, continuing to expose sensitive context fields.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "All three sinks directly interpolate and print the raw `event[\"context\"]`, causing any present API keys or secrets to be written verbatim into logs, metric tags, or error tracker payloads.",
      "at": "errors.py:9, logfile.py:8, metrics.py:6",
      "call": "`python run.py` with an event payload where `event[\"context\"]` contains a sensitive key like `{\"api_key\": \"sk_live_...\"}`",
      "defect": "Unsanitized data rendering / credential leakage risk",
      "expected": "The sinks should strip, mask, or redact sensitive context fields before serialization to comply with the security rule."
    }
  ]
}
